From: ae-automation-bot <ae-automation-bot@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 19:20:22 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 130/148] [ae-patch] Show a failed subagent under its own
 Failed group in the rail and the Agents tab
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A Claude Code subagent that failed read as finished. The child list built
each row's status only from the in-memory status cache, so after a server
restart a failed child read idle although its row's live_status still said
failed; the summary now falls back to that persisted failure on a cache miss.
On the web, splitAgentSections returns failed rows in their own list; the
Agents tab and the rail's Agents section both show them in an always-open
Failed group with Tabler's alert-triangle icon, and the rail summary reads
"1 running · 1 failed · 2 finished", leaving out zero parts. The rail now
reads its subagent rows from the same live child list as the Agents tab
(useChildSessions, kept current by the session stream) instead of its own
60 s poll, so the two agree. Elapsed time still counts from the first
launch: a resume leaves no trace in the child's items or summary.
